-## Brand build (house flag)
-`src/hb3d/brand.js` (embedded after `viewer.js`) puts the brand book's build animation and hologram look (brand handover 6.2 to 6.10) on every clean model, for the Level 1 deposit build only. It is off unless the app calls `viewer.setBrand(true)`, which it does with `?house=new` or `localStorage['vi-flag-house'] = '1'` (`hbBrandOn()` in index.html; `?house=old` forces it off for a visit). With the flag off the viewer behaves exactly as before.
+## Brand build (the only house builder)
+`src/hb3d/brand.js` (embedded after `viewer.js`) puts the brand book's build animation and hologram look (brand handover 6.2 to 6.10) on every clean model. Since 1 Nov 2026 (owner: "completely delete this old version") it is the only house builder: there is no house flag, no Settings switch and no classic viewer; the app always calls `viewer.setBrand(true)`. `viewer.js` keeps only what the brand build needs (renderer, camera, controls, frame loop, the faint block context for flats, edges, focus box).
 
 - **Money to bricks.** `HB3D.brandBrickValue(depositTarget, bricksTotal) = depositTarget * 0.77 / bricksTotal`; `HB3D.brandBricksLaid(bricksTotal, p) = floor(bricksTotal * seg(p, 0.03, 0.80))`. Each model keeps its own brick total (`model.counts.bricks`) and row count (`model.rows.n`).
 - **Laying plan.** `HB3D.brandPlan(model)` (pure, cached on the model) orders the bricks course by course, then round the ring (front, right, back, left), using the per-instance kind the kit writes (`batch.kind`: 1 brick, 2 tile, 3 block). Trim (sills, lintels, mortar beds, stone, bay roofs) shows with the first brick of its course; roof tiles go on eaves to ridge from 0.80 to 0.88; frames, glass and doors fade in from 0.88 to 0.93; glass warms 0.93 to 0.96; the door turns gold 0.96 to 1; keys glint at 0.999. `HB3D.brandStats(model, p)` gives bricks and tiles laid, the row (course of the last brick laid, or of the roof once tiles go on; every row from 0.88), the slice height and the stage name. The HUD, caption, statistics card and 3D tag all read it.
 - **Viewer.** Brand meshes are separate instanced meshes with a small shader: drop 6 courses (0.45 m) over 0.38 s with an e^3 ease, fade in, gold flash 1.1 s, a stagger of min(0.12 s, 0.9 s / n) for 60 bricks or fewer, instant un-laying; far faces faint, near faces 88%, mortar bevel, 2.8 s pulse, a sweep band at 20 courses a second. The last brick laid sits 14% proud in pale gold. Environment: stage gradient, fading 11-line grid, ground glow, dashed site boundary and footprint (0 to 0.03), 18 rafters per roof (0.60 to 0.80), ring ping from the base, the gold slice (fades from 0.97), auto orbit that yields to a touch for 2.5 s. Displayed progress eases with `p += (target - p) * min(1, dt * 1.7)`; opening the tab builds from 0.
 - **Reduced motion** (`prefers-reduced-motion` or `body.reduced-motion`): instant build, no drop, flash, stagger, sweep, ring or orbit, pulse held at its midpoint, and the loop sleeps once drawn. Rendering stops when the stage is off screen; pixel ratio is capped at 1.5 below 700 px and 2 above. A device whose frames average slower than 1/10 s drops to a lite stage (pixel ratio 1, no ambient motion, draws only while building).
-- Level 2 (equity), Level 3 (upgrade) and uploaded designs keep the current look. Tests: `tests/test_hb_brand.js` (`VI_INDEX=/path/index.html` runs it against another copy).
+- **Level 2** (owner, 1 Nov 2026). `equity` (paying the mortgage): the whole house laid at once, the paid share solid below a gold line at `waterline()` (the `uCut` uniform; fragments above it are discarded) and a faint hologram pass above it (`BRAND_HOLO`, `VP._brandHolo`, sharing the same meshes); the line eases up as payments come in with a gold flash band under it (`uRise`, 1.1 s); gold tag "MORTGAGE x% PAID". `complete` (mortgage free): all solid, windows lit, door gold, tag "MORTGAGE FREE".
+- **Speed** (owner, 31 Oct 2026). Parts that have landed move into one static mesh per part (`BRAND_STATIC`, baked in 4 ms idle slices, page copy dropped after upload, at most 640,000 vertices a house; bigger parts stay instanced); the overlays write only what changed; 30 frames a second at rest. `tests/test_hb_speed.js`.
+- **Level 3 and uploaded designs** are locked under Pro for everyone (owner, 1 Nov 2026); their code is dormant and nothing draws them.
+- **No 3D** (no WebGL, old device, three.js blocked or offline): `hbStill()` in index.html draws a still picture of the same house at its current build level on a 2D canvas from `brandPlan` (no three.js), with the same HUD figures.
+- Tests: `tests/test_hb_brand.js`, `tests/test_hb_one_builder.js`, `tests/test_hb_speed.js` (`VI_INDEX=/path/index.html` runs them against another copy).
